    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Historically, North River was one of the centers of the New York State garnet industry.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/North_River%2C_New_York"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The last remaining garnet mine in New York is located in North River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/North_River%2C_New_York"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The hardest garnets in the world come from the Adirondacks and are still in demand, especially for industrial use.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/North_River%2C_New_York"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The former garnet mine, Hooper Mine, now serves as a tourist site.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/North_River%2C_New_York"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "A local attraction is Gore Mountain, one of the tallest in New York and a skiing center.",
